WEBVTT

00:00:20.195 --> 00:00:21.730
[belches]

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:02.482
[music stops]
[people shouting]

00:01:02.586 --> 00:01:03.878
[yelling]

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.239
[yelps]

00:01:05.239 --> 00:01:06.239
[growls]
Olé!

00:01:06.714 --> 00:01:07.971
[grunts]

00:01:13.472 --> 00:01:15.747
[muffled grunting]

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:19.720
[yells]

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.820
So, should we get out of here?
Yeah, time to go.

00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:27.632
[laughing]
That was amazing!

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:29.129
Wait a second.
Did we even pay our tab?

00:01:29.309 --> 00:01:30.309
It doesn't matter!

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:32.409
Watch this, watch this.
I always wanted to do this.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.175
[laughs]

00:01:36.288 --> 00:01:39.256
Get 'em!
See ya, suckers!

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.009
I can't say for sure,
but I think they liked me.

00:01:43.259 --> 00:01:45.510
[man] Come on!
Don't let 'em get away!

00:01:45.635 --> 00:01:47.344
[all yelling]

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:49.310
Oh, yes!
[laughs] Yeah!

00:01:49.570 --> 00:01:50.730
Yes!
Ouch!

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:51.970
He got you pretty good.

00:01:52.030 --> 00:01:53.350
I'm all right.
I've been hit harder.

00:01:53.650 --> 00:01:55.170
Did you see how much
toilet paper I used?

00:01:55.209 --> 00:01:58.589
The next person that goes
into that bathroom
will have nothing to wipe with!

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:01.850
The floors were sticky.
The crowd was rough.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.490
And the odds
were against us.

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:06.570
But there was no stopping
Donut Lord and the Blue Blur.

00:02:07.029 --> 00:02:09.169
Scratch another one
off my list.

00:02:10.529 --> 00:02:12.189
You are a weird little dude.

00:02:16.925 --> 00:02:18.477
[groans]

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:23.180
Mmm.

00:02:23.180 --> 00:02:23.982
Mmm.

00:02:23.982 --> 00:02:24.784
Mmm.

00:02:24.784 --> 00:02:25.360
Mmm.

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:26.160
Okay.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.380
So what are we gonna do now?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:32.500
I'm gonna pass out watching TV.
I think you should too.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.000
But this is my
last night on Earth.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:35.879
I want to soak up
every last second.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:38.180
All right, well, anything you
can find to do in this room,

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.220
you knock yourself out.

00:02:43.566 --> 00:02:45.129
[shower running]

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.420
Good times.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:51.680
[farts]
Oh, come on.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.160
[groans] That's awful.
What did you eat?

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.600
I think it's called a chili dog?

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:59.120
You might want to check
your fur on that one, buddy.

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:03.420
Hey. So, what's this next planet
you're supposed to go to like?

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:05.500
It's no Earth,
I can tell you that.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:08.020
There's no people,
just breathable air

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.620
and giant mushrooms and stuff.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.400
Well, look at it this way.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.239
At least you won't be
the only "fun-guy."

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.620
No. Don't ever do that again.

00:03:17.721 --> 00:03:18.899
[chuckles]

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.000
I liked it.

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.710
I'm really gonna
miss this place.

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.489
I know I have to
leave Earth to be safe,

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:28.030
but what if
Longclaw was wrong?

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:30.890
Maybe I could have a life here.

00:03:35.830 --> 00:03:38.270
All right.
We should get some sleep.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:41.430
You sleep.
Don't worry about me.

00:03:41.489 --> 00:03:44.470
I'm gonna stay up all night
enjoying Earth while I can.

00:03:45.089 --> 00:03:46.089
Sure, kid.

00:03:46.196 --> 00:03:48.600
As long as we're
on the road by 8:00.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:53.945
[snores, murmuring]

00:03:55.022 --> 00:03:57.964
[murmurs]
I ate a chili dog.
That's why my farts smell.

00:04:13.069 --> 00:04:17.289
Thomas Wachowski,
accused of committing
an act of domestic terrorism.

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:20.330
Wachowski is considered
armed and dangerous.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:22.629
Any information
regarding his whereabouts

00:04:22.629 --> 00:04:25.209
should be reported to
local authorities immediately.

00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:33.059
Did he say where he was going?

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:38.880
Maybe. Maybe not.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.380
Like I'd ever tell you.

00:04:43.099 --> 00:04:44.460
Stand down, Agent Stone.

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:48.680
This well-meaning citizen
obviously doesn't understand
the urgency of the matter.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:52.930
Really?

00:04:54.145 --> 00:04:55.145
[yells]

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.718
[Robotnik] Now that's
what I call good cop, bad cop.

00:04:57.718 --> 00:04:59.144
[chuckles]

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:00.680
Hoy!
[gags]

00:05:01.059 --> 00:05:02.239
Left yourself open.

00:05:02.364 --> 00:05:05.234
[gasps]

00:05:05.359 --> 00:05:07.319
Judging by the quickest route
to San Francisco,

00:05:07.479 --> 00:05:08.839
the approximate
speed of their vehicle,

00:05:09.339 --> 00:05:10.580
and local weather conditions...

00:05:10.682 --> 00:05:12.016
[tapping console]

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.939
They should be...

00:05:14.599 --> 00:05:17.299
right about...

00:05:17.299 --> 00:05:18.299
here.

00:05:18.779 --> 00:05:21.419
That's brilliant, sir.
Thanks...

00:05:21.519 --> 00:05:22.519
[whispers]
for nothing.

00:05:22.709 --> 00:05:25.619
[engine revs]

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.770
So, what's on your bucket list?Who, me?

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.610
Yeah. Everyone has
a bucket list, right?

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:30.710
Sure, but...

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.690
I mean, you're the one
leaving Earth, and...

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.750
I'm not planning
on dying anytime soon.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:36.270
[chuckles]
Don't be so sure.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.290
Your best friend
is a magnet for danger.

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.170
Are you anointing yourself
as the bestie?

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.550
Mm-hmm.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:44.010
A little presumptuous, but...
I mean... What, no...

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:46.230
I like you, of course, but,

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:47.770
you know,
we're not best friends.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.830
You tucked me in last night.
[snorts]

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:52.370
Fine, fine, fine.
Best animal friend.

00:05:52.450 --> 00:05:53.750
That would be my dog, Ozzy.
Okay...

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:57.330
let's drop
this increasingly humiliating
topic of conversation.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.130
Bucket list.
Give it to me!

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.690
Okay, there is one thing.

00:06:02.670 --> 00:06:04.430
In Green Hills,
I've always felt,

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.490
I don't know,
more like a babysitter
than a real cop, you know?

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:11.330
So I want a chance
to prove myself,
under real pressure.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:13.910
I'm gonna move to San Francisco,
become a street cop.

00:06:14.710 --> 00:06:17.330
And, I don't know,
see if I have what it takes.

00:06:18.590 --> 00:06:19.590
What?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.350
Why--
Why is your face doing that?

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.110
You're leaving Green Hills?

00:06:24.661 --> 00:06:26.079
Okay.

00:06:26.196 --> 00:06:28.952
B-B-But why?
Why would you leave Green Hills?

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.730
This may be hard
for you to understand,
but Green Hills is a small town.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:32.870
It's a very small town.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.850
Uh, it's not small.
There are hundreds of people.

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.390
That's a small town, dude!

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.250
It's a perfect town,
and the people need you.

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:41.970
Please.
I clean out their gutters.

00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.850
I jump-start their cars
in the winter.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.310
They could call anybody
to do that.

00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.730
Sure, they can call anybody,
but they don't.

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:49.230
They call you.

00:06:51.694 --> 00:06:55.098
[machinery powering up]

00:06:59.597 --> 00:07:01.828
[beeping]

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:08.560
[sighs]
Eeny, meeny, miny...

00:07:09.980 --> 00:07:10.682
mayhem.

00:07:10.682 --> 00:07:12.194
[chuckles]

